	doi = {10.1109/ICMCSI64620.2025.10883443},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105000007703?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {MARK-1 proposes the development of an autonomous navigational walker aimed at improving patient care and safety within healthcare environments. The primary objective is to improve the quality of life for individuals with mobility limitations by providing seamless mobility support and integrated medical assistance. Key features of the proposed walker-structured robot includes robust safety mechanisms for obstacle detection and avoidance, personalized adaptability to individual user needs, and a user-friendly interface for intuitive control. The proposed robot is engineered to navigate various indoor terrains effortlessly, ensuring reliable mobility across diverse environments. Integration of health monitoring functionalities, such as tracking patient’s progress, delivering food and water essentials to patients, tele-assistance on video call, constant surveillance, and fall detection, enhances the system's capability to provide timely assistance and emergency response. The autonomous navigational walker proposed, potentially contributes to improved quality of life for individuals with mobility limitations. © 2025 IEEE.},
