	abstract = {This work provides the design and implementation of a voice-powered wheelchair for helping people with physical disabilities to enhance mobility and autonomy. The wheelchair combines different assistive technologies using a Raspberry Pi as the main controller and enables motorized movement by voice commands, fall detection, and obstacle avoidance. Directional control is done through voice commands, enabling natural hands-free movement forward, backwards, left and right. Obstacle detection is done by ultrasonic sensors that will detect if there are objects near the system and thus prevent it from colliding with them. An emergency alert is included that provides a buzzer trigger and an emergency message that is sent to the designated contact. A medication alert feature is included in the system, which provides an audible alert through a buzzer and sends a notification to the user’s mobile, reminding them of the scheduled time to take their medication. The proposed system is said to hold potential applications in the healthcare and rehabilitation sectors, supporting greater independence and improving the quality of life of individuals. The results obtained from this work include reliable and accurate voice recognition for wheelchair navigation, efficient obstacle detection ensuring collision-free movement, and timely alerts for emergencies and medication schedules. Overall, the system achieved an average success rate of approximately 95% for different possible scenarios, demonstrating its effectiveness and reliability in real-world conditions. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2027.},
