	abstract = {The risk of falls amongst wheelchair-bound and paralyzed patients is a serious health concern, as they have restricted mobility and are often unable to reach help much later than anyone else. Most fall detection systems operate with ambulatory users in mind, which do not correctly capture critical wheelchair-specific fall scenarios, such as the wheelchair tilting over, sliding of the wheelchair, or transferring incidents in general. This paper proposes an AI-IoT hybrid framework for wheelchair user-specific automated fall detection. Wearable and wheelchair-mounted IoT sensors are combined with a hybrid deep learning model that integrates Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (BiLSTM), and Attention mechanisms. An edge-cloud architecture enables real-time inference and adaptive learning. Experimental results achieved a fall detection accuracy of 96.4%, yielding a high reduction in false alarms during normal operation of the wheelchair. The proposed framework offers a reliable and scalable solution for smart healthcare and assisted living environments.  © 2026 IEEE.},
