	abstract = {Aiming at the issues of limited recognition accuracy and high false alarm rates in existing fall detection systems, this paper designs a fall detection system based on a smart cane. The system uses the ESP32-S3 as the main controller, collects the user's motion and physiological data in real-time through the MPU6050 attitude sensor and the MAX30102 physiological sensor, and optimizes the data locally. A multi-level threshold fusion algorithm is employed for fall judgment. This paper proposes a hierarchical recognition algorithm that integrates motion and physiological signals with interactive confirmation, combining multidimensional information such as attitude angle, acceleration, heart rate, and blood oxygen to categorize fall scenarios into three types, thereby improving detection accuracy and reducing the false alarm rate through interactive confirmation. Results from 500 simulated action experiments show that the system achieves a fall recognition accuracy of 97.2%, significantly reducing the false alarm rate. Additionally, the system features low cost and high real-time performance. This study provides an efficient hardware implementation solution and algorithmic approach for real-time and accurate fall detection. © 2026 SPIE.},
